    "created_at": "2026-08-14T16:14:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-14T16:14:11Z",
    "body": "This was unfortunately rejected at the time in https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/35855, see the comment https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/35855#issuecomment-4121829556.\r\n\r\nHowever, since then, MXFP8 emulation was added in https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/45381 that added:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/03a8d0b1ede68efc20b8bbfc14ee4681a62f8d75/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/emulation.py#L36-L48\r\n\r\nthat is strictly the same thing as https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/35855 wanted to achieve.\r\n\r\nOverall, I don't see an issue in mirroring https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/45381 approach, but the correct place would be: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/03a8d0b1ede68efc20b8bbfc14ee4681a62f8d75/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp4/emulation.py#L99-L100\r\n\r\nThis is independent of Quark checkpoints (should be compatible with mxfp4.py/compressed-tensors/modelopt/online/etc).\r\n\r\nIn general, I think we should also just add a fused mxfp4 dequant + BF16 GEMM kernel (e.g. flydsl) that would be much faster than current emulation (e.g. if running on gfx942):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/03a8d0b1ede68efc20b8bbfc14ee4681a62f8d75/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/__init__.py#L561-L564\r\n\r\nI did prototype similar nvfp4 dequant + BF16 GEMM kernel on gfx950 and performance is decent",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
